 701:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_adc.c ****   *         all ADC instances use the same core clock at RCC level, disabling
 702:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_adc.c ****   *         the core clock reset all ADC instances).
 703:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_adc.c ****   *         If this is not the case, reset of these common parameters reset is
 704:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_adc.c ****   *         bypassed without error reporting: it can be the intended behavior in
 705:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_adc.c ****   *         case of reset of a single ADC while the other ADCs sharing the same
 706:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_adc.c ****   *         common group is still running.
 707:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_adc.c ****   * @note   By default, HAL_ADC_DeInit() set ADC in mode deep power-down:
 708:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_adc.c ****   *         this saves more power by reducing leakage currents
 709:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_adc.c ****   *         and is particularly interesting before entering MCU low-power modes.
 710:platform/HAL/src/stm32g4xx_hal_adc.c ****   * @param hadc ADC handle
